'''Level 4''',<ref name="Companion">{{InsiderCite|217|Star Wars: Andor Season One Companion|''Star Wars: Andor'' Season One Companion}}</ref> also known as '''Four''', was one of the<ref name="Andor9" /> eight levels<ref name="Andor10">{{Andor|One Way Out}}</ref> in [[Narkina 5 Imperial Prison Complex|one]] of the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Prison]] Complexes on<ref name="Andor9" /> the [[moon]]<ref name="Episode8Audio">{{Andor|Narkina 5 (episode)}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> [[Narkina 5]].<ref name="Andor9" /> In [[5 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{AndorDate|109}}</ref> a [[prisoner]] from four was mistakenly transferred to [[unit two-five]] on [[Level 2 (Narkina 5)|Level 2]] after finishing his sentence, instead of being sent to another facility, revealing to the prisoners in the unit that they would never be released, only transferred elsewhere. The Imperials used the prison's electrified flooring to kill all one hundred men in the unit to keep them quiet,<ref name="Andor9" /> but word still ultimately got out and led to the other prisoners [[Narkina 5 prison escape|rising up]] and taking over the prison before escaping.<ref name="Andor10" />

